1.1.text:
REGARDING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION
FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF SOUTH BANGKA,
Considering : a. that the number of violence against women and children in South Bangka has experienced an increase in the number of incidents. Meanwhile, protection and services for victims have been provided but are still not optimal;
b. that in South Bangka Regency, an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children (P2TP2A) for victims of violence has been established, but the basis for its establishment still uses a Regent Regulation which does not yet include the mechanism or implementation of protection that can facilitate victims and protection providers in carrying it out;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation regarding the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 4 of 1979 regarding Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
3143);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 regarding Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 5 of 1998 regarding Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1998 Number 164, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3783);
5. Law Number 23 of 2002 regarding Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
6. Law Number 5 of 2003 regarding the Establishment of South Bangka Regency, Central Bangka Regency, West Bangka Regency, and East Belitung Regency in the Province of Bangka Belitung Islands (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 25, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4268);
7. Law Number 23 of 2004 regarding the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 13 of 2006 regarding Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
9. Law Number 21 of 2007 regarding the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
10. Law Number 12 of 2011 regarding the Formation of Laws and Regulations (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
11. Law Number 23 of 2014 regarding Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
12. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 regarding the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
With Mutual Agreement

CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTIONS ORGANIZING PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS
Article 13
(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children (P2TP2A) as the Organizing Institution for the integrated prevention and protection of women and children who are victims of violence.
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of:
a. health;
b. law enforcement;
c. social affairs and empowerment;
d. education and religious affairs;
e. Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs); and
f. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 8
Every victim has the right to receive:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal services;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage; and
e. confidential handling, whether for an individual, group, or institution, whether governmental or non-governmental.

