REGARDING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION
FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF SOUTH BANGKA,
Considering : a. that the number of violence against women and children in South Bangka has experienced an increase in the number of incidents. Meanwhile, protection and services for victims have been provided but are still not optimal;
b. that in South Bangka Regency, an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children (P2TP2A) for victims of violence has been established, but the basis for its establishment still uses a Regent Regulation which does not yet include the mechanism or implementation of protection that can facilitate victims and protection providers in carrying it out;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation regarding the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
