7.3.text:
CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTIONS ORGANIZING PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS
Article 13
(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children (P2TP2A) as the Organizing Institution for the integrated prevention and protection of women and children who are victims of violence.
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements of:
a. health;
b. law enforcement;
c. social affairs and empowerment;
d. education and religious affairs;
e. Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs); and
f. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

